@startuml
title Darija Translator — Deployment Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho

node "Windows workstation" as Workstation {
  node "Terminal" as Terminal {
    artifact "Python CLI\ndarija_translate.py" as Python
  }

  node "PHP development server\nphp -S 127.0.0.1:8081" as PhpServer {
    artifact "PHP web client\nindex.php" as Php
  }
  node "Web browser" as PhpBrowser

  node "Chrome 116+" as Chrome {
    artifact "MV3 service worker" as Worker
    artifact "Side panel" as Panel
    database "chrome.storage.local\nbackend URL + username" as LocalStorage
    database "chrome.storage.session\npassword + pending selection" as SessionStorage
  }
}

node "Physical iPhone" as IPhone {
  node "Expo Go SDK 58" {
    artifact "React Native client\npassword in component state only" as Mobile
  }
}

node "Backend host" as BackendHost {
  artifact "Process environment — backend only\nTRANSLATOR_DEMO_USERNAME / TRANSLATOR_DEMO_PASSWORD\nkeystore_password\nGEMINI_API_KEY\nGEMINI_MODEL / base URL / timeout" as Environment

  node "Open Liberty / Java 17\nHTTP endpoint :9080" as Liberty {
    component "Jakarta Authentication\nBasicAuthenticationModule" as Authentication
    component "Jakarta REST API\nGET /api/health (public)\nPOST /api/translate (protected)" as RestApi
    component "GeminiTranslationClient\nJDK HttpClient" as GeminiClient
  }
}

cloud "Google Gemini Developer API" as Gemini

PhpBrowser --> Php : HTTP form GET / POST
Worker --> SessionStorage : selected text
Worker --> Panel : opens side panel
Panel --> LocalStorage : reads/writes URL + username
Panel --> SessionStorage : reads/writes runtime password

Python --> RestApi : HTTP/JSON\nGET /api/health
Python --> Authentication : HTTP/JSON + Basic authentication\nPOST /api/translate
Php --> Authentication : HTTP/JSON + Basic authentication\nPOST /api/translate
Panel --> Authentication : HTTP/JSON + Basic authentication\nPOST /api/translate
Mobile --> Authentication : HTTP/JSON + Basic authentication\nPOST /api/translate over LAN

Authentication --> RestApi : valid translator-user
RestApi --> GeminiClient : validated text + source language
Environment --> Authentication : backend credentials
Environment --> GeminiClient : server-side key + settings
GeminiClient --> Gemini : HTTPS/JSON\nPOST /v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent\nx-goog-api-key

note bottom of Python
  Clients submit backend credentials only.
  No client receives or stores GEMINI_API_KEY.
end note
note bottom of Mobile
  The iPhone reaches the backend by its LAN URL.
  The masked password is runtime-only.
end note
@enduml
